","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"cIzp7QZOaUyRLl3ZcwsrHw","review_id":"WFXnvPlLzvmGr_0ukUHYcg","date":"2020-11-30T22:08:33","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9555229544639587,"text_excerpt":"We got a gift card for Addis Nola and got takeout recently. I was so pleased and surprised! I love Ethiopian food, but I'm critical because my very first Ethiopian restaurant (Meskerem in St. Louis, stop and eat there some day) is far and away my favorite and Its difficult for other places to match up for me. But Addis was wonderful, filling and delicious! I got the Veggie combo (vegetarians! this is a must!) and enjoyed it thoroughly. I was disappointed that my cabbage and carrot dish didn't have potatoes in it (which it purports to do, and which I have had before at different establishments), but was still thrilled with everything else. The injera was also delicious and plentiful. My pa..."},{"business_id":"cIzp7QZOaUyRLl3ZcwsrHw","review_id":"p5KAsrKPBDnez17v83ai-g","date":"2021-05-19T03:21:11","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9449812769889832,"text_excerpt":"Addis has some of the best Ethiopian food. Period. Not in New Orleans. But anywhere. The staff is friendly and welcoming to newcomers and I highly encourage anyone curious to check it out. Especially if you have friends that think vegetarian food can't be good - the vegetable combo from here will dissuade any notions of that. It's hard to go wrong with anything on the menu here - from the lamb tibs to the kitfo to the doro wot it's all a delight. Hell, I'd be happy eating just the injera."},{"business_id":"cIzp7QZOaUyRLl3ZcwsrHw","review_id":"rF86y27l_oejvzBjhKAOFw","date":"2019-05-18T17:08:20","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9428887963294983,"text_excerpt":"I've been wanting to try Ethiopian food for a while so I am very pleased I now have an easily accessible option here in the city. My boyfriend and I went on a Tuesday eve so there wasn't a huge crowd. I was familiar with the location since I used to frequent a different restaurant that was previously located there. The parking lot is a little weird and difficult to get out of as there is no real turn around area. Also the ambiance is kind of lacking but that's ok because the food was phenomenal. I had the whole tilapia with collard greens and it was so good. Also the appetizer, I forgot the name of it, but it's similar to a Jamaican meat pie, it was excellent. Everything was hot and very ..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"cIzp7QZOaUyRLl3ZcwsrHw","photo_id":"3OjbJlDBKVon-82dVqvWgg","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/3OjbJlDBKVon-82dVqvWgg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8953348398208618},{"business_id":"cIzp7QZOaUyRLl3ZcwsrHw","photo_id":"X_eJNFtk5x4jzpRLKpqOng","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/X_eJNFtk5x4jzpRLKpqOng.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8340756893157959},{"business_id":"cIzp7QZOaUyRLl3ZcwsrHw","photo_id":"C1kMaRAYh5cCOL_xbj1MZQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/C1kMaRAYh5cCOL_xbj1MZQ.jpg","visual_